From: ephico2real2 <ephico2real@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:35:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ztunnel/zds: require bounded explicit acknowledgments and
 retire canceled streams

Reject missing ACKs and unsupported protocol versions. Carry caller cancellation through queued updates, discard expired requests, and retire ambiguous in-flight streams so late ACKs cannot credit the next operation. Join replaced handlers and commit cache state before publishing success. Release the snapshot cache lock before network I/O and log actual acknowledged enrollment.

Local Linux ARM64 qualification: race-enabled real-socket cancellation, timeout, replacement and shutdown cases; privileged network namespace/iptables/rolling update suite; Go vet and repository golangci-lint pass. This does not yet make CNI admission or namespace transitions fail closed. Tracks CMTC issue12. CI is deferred.

Signed-off-by: ephico2real2 <ephico2real@gmail.com>
